        "modelingNotes": [
          "Exact Siemens order-number candidate. Abbreviated CPU family names do not establish this order number or hardware revision. Review the selected hardware before use.",
          "All 38 assigned X10/X11/X12 field terminals are inventoried. X10.1/.2 are the CPU power inputs. X10.4/.5 are sensor supply outputs, not power inputs. X11 uses gold connectors.",
          "14 digital inputs, 10 relay outputs, two 0-10 V analog inputs and two 0-20 mA analog outputs. Ratings are descriptive; load category, output commons, input reference wiring, power budget, firmware and installation conditions require review.",
          "Two PROFINET RJ45 sockets belong to interface X1; X1.P1 and X1.P2 are normalized port keys. Memory-card, optional signal-board and expansion/backplane connectors are not modeled.",
          "Channel functions identify I/O endpoints. Relay common/contact behavior, CPU electronics, analog reference and sensor-supply connections do not create physical continuity or implied energization.",
          "Manufacturer web cross-check: https://docs.tia.siemens.cloud/r/simatic_s7_1200_manual_collection_enus_20/technical-specifications/cpu-1215c/cpu-1215c-wiring-diagrams ; V20 tables 1-2, publication 11/2024.",
          "thermite:io-module supports the single-terminal I/O symbols. The AC supply function is not supported by the original continuous profile; use terminal-wiring views for its explicit power terminals. Unsupported functions must remain visible as renderer diagnostics."
        ]
      },
